1
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,598
Ermes, call a doctor.

2
00:00:15,682 --> 00:00:18,768
- The doctors should be back to normal.
- Jolyne…

3
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:20,812
- Emporio!
- Jolyne!

4
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:24,816
The wind has stopped blowing.

5
00:00:25,942 --> 00:00:29,195
The rainbows are gone, Jolyne.

6
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:35,326
He was truly happy the last few days.

7
00:00:35,994 --> 00:00:38,496
Weather was already saved!

8
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,298
I wish…

9
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:52,886
I wish we can talk just one more time.

10
00:00:55,680 --> 00:01:00,226
I want to talk to you
in the warm breeze again.

11
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:19,370
MARCH 21ST, 2012 - 10:35 AM

12
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:22,665
TWO MORE DAYS UNTIL THE NEW MOON

13
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:30,548
Weather Forecast…

14
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:34,511
He didn't want me to despair,

15
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:37,931
and wanted to tell me
to keep going after the priest.

16
00:01:38,431 --> 00:01:40,433
So he used Pale Snake's ability

17
00:01:40,975 --> 00:01:44,354
to leave his own ability in a disc.

18
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:49,776
If I insert this disc into my head,

19
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,445
would I be able to use his ability?

20
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:57,992
But the priest is already
on his way to Cape Canaveral.

21
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:01,204
We don't even have two days
until the new moon.

22
00:02:02,163 --> 00:02:03,164
It could well be

23
00:02:04,165 --> 00:02:07,627
that this is already out of my hands.

24
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:11,548
What should I do?

25
00:02:13,049 --> 00:02:14,968
Despite the snail commotion,

26
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:18,346
my father's disc is now in
the Speedwagon Foundation's hands.

27
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:21,766
My father will wake up sooner or later.

28
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:24,561
He would know what to do.

29
00:02:24,644 --> 00:02:27,147
Should I wait for him?

30
00:02:27,772 --> 00:02:33,444
But the priest may take drastic measures
in Cape Canaveral before Dad wakes up.

31
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:38,491
What should I do?

32
00:02:40,201 --> 00:02:43,705
Dad, tell me.

33
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:45,582
Had I not gotten in the car,

34
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:48,585
would Weather still be alive?

35
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:51,629
No, I have to keep moving forward.

36
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:53,381
I have to go to Cape Canaveral.

37
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:55,425
I have to defeat the priest.

38
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:57,927
Dad, tell me.

39
00:02:58,428 --> 00:03:01,556
What can someone like me do?

40
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:03,474
What can I do?

41
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:47,745
EPISODE 33: GRAVITY OF THE NEW MOON

42
00:04:50,498 --> 00:04:53,084
How cute.

43
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:54,127
Wow.

44
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:57,505
She looks adorable.

45
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:03,136
Jolyne fell asleep on my shoulder!

46
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,805
That's right.

47
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:08,182
I finally found you.

48
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:10,935
There's something I meant to tell you

49
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:13,980
if I managed to break out of prison
and find you.

50
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:16,357
I don't have time to waste.

51
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:18,901
If I don't say this now, then when?

52
00:05:19,652 --> 00:05:21,696
My feelings are honest and true.

53
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:26,492
I spent a fortune buying this ring
from the prison scrounger.

54
00:05:26,993 --> 00:05:28,953
Once you wake up,

55
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:34,083
please accept my love for you.

56
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:37,211
Hey, look!

57
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:41,215
Alligators! They're this far inland!

58
00:05:41,299 --> 00:05:42,967
Dammit.

59
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:48,639
They may be a protected species,
but they sure gave us hell in prison!

60
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:51,142
Seriously? Whoa, massive alligators.

61
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:53,936
Take this, dumbass!

62
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,397
Woo-hoo, I got one!

63
00:05:57,565 --> 00:06:00,401
They reacted! They're startled!

64
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:02,278
They're not moving, but they're scared.

65
00:06:02,361 --> 00:06:04,447
Don't mess with us, you overgrown lizards!

66
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:05,782
Dumbasses!

67
00:06:06,699 --> 00:06:07,784
You couldn't have…

68
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:09,535
Jolyne!

69
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:11,287
What did you throw just now?

70
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:16,250
Show it to me. Show me your hand!

71
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:17,919
What's with you?

72
00:06:18,002 --> 00:06:20,254
What's all this shouting?

73
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:23,382
I said, open your hand!

74
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:24,467
What the hell?

75
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:27,178
Anastasia, why are you excited?

76
00:06:27,261 --> 00:06:28,679
You…

77
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:33,851
You couldn't have! You can't have!

78
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:44,695
Ermes.

79
00:06:44,779 --> 00:06:47,031
- Can you do me a favor?
- What is it?

80
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:49,867
I want to see the map for this area.

81
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,911
Can you hold onto this for me?

82
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:53,287
Sure.

83
00:06:56,749 --> 00:07:00,795
When you say map, you mean GPS, right?

84
00:07:01,337 --> 00:07:03,089
This is such an old computer.

85
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:09,387
This is our current location,
Cape Canaveral.

86
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:12,056
North latitude, 28 degrees 24 minutes,

87
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:14,475
west longitude, 80 degrees 36 minutes.

88
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:17,270
Cape Canaveral is on the Florida Peninsula
by the Atlantic Ocean.

89
00:07:17,353 --> 00:07:20,857
It's a vast area of 34,000 hectares.

90
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:23,401
It's a sandbank formed by nature
over a long time.

91
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:24,652
Sandbank?

92
00:07:25,236 --> 00:07:28,364
It's a geological feature
formed by sand deposits.

93
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:31,659
This is our destination.

94
00:07:31,742 --> 00:07:33,703
The Space Center.

95
00:07:34,287 --> 00:07:35,955
There are no trains or buses.

96
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:39,083
You can only access the facility
by car, either owned or rented.

97
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,669
This is where they launch
rockets, satellites,

98
00:07:41,752 --> 00:07:44,589
and test space shuttles.

99
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:47,717
That's the space shuttle assembly factory.

100
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:50,470
Over here is the launch site and lookout.

101
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:52,722
Each facility is
more than five kilometers apart.

102
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:53,973
That's how big this place is.

103
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,809
We will enter through the Visitor Center.

104
00:07:57,310 --> 00:08:00,938
All general admission
has to come in through here.

105
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:04,942
We'll buy the tickets,
pass through security,

106
00:08:05,026 --> 00:08:06,944
and then hop on the tour bus.

107
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:11,157
The other areas are off-limits,

108
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:15,161
so this must be the same route
the priest would take.

109
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:17,830
I don't know what he wants to do here,

110
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:20,875
but I believe he will spend
the remaining days until the new moon

111
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:24,086
somewhere inside the Space Center.

112
00:08:26,088 --> 00:08:27,673
No more.

113
00:08:28,424 --> 00:08:32,011
Due to security concerns,
we are limiting the number of visitors.

114
00:08:32,094 --> 00:08:33,763
Please wait in line.

115
00:08:34,805 --> 00:08:37,099
Oh, but he's with me.

116
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:39,185
You'll let him slide, right?

117
00:08:39,268 --> 00:08:40,436
Sure.

118
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:42,480
Now, come along.

119
00:08:47,735 --> 00:08:50,863
You would've had to wait
another 15 minutes.

120
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:55,618
Are you a pastor? Or a priest?

121
00:08:56,202 --> 00:09:00,414
I'm trying to do small acts of kindness
in my everyday life.

122
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:01,874
Are you a tourist?

123
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:06,921
Do clergymen have an interest in rockets?

124
00:09:07,004 --> 00:09:09,507
You just seem out of place.

125
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:13,469
Actually, I kind of understand.
God and space.

126
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:14,470
How symbolic.

127
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:19,642
Would you be offended if I asked
if God was an alien?

128
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:24,939
Do I have to tolerate
your incessant questions?

129
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:29,026
You did a good deed,
so you can leave me alone now.

130
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:32,780
If you're bored of waiting in line,
go waste your time somewhere else.

131
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:38,160
I didn't come here
just to rush for 15 minutes.

132
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:50,381
Gravity is the biggest obstacle
when launching a rocket.

133
00:09:50,965 --> 00:09:53,676
Ideally, a rocket can launch most easily

134
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:56,470
if there is less
gravitational pull upon it.

135
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:59,515
That's why launching a rocket
along the equator 

136
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:02,560
 gives it an advantage over gravity.

137
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:05,313
This is because
the Earth's centrifugal force

138
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:09,358
causes gravity to weaken
along the equator.

139
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:15,323
Athletes may be able to break
their records near the equator.

140
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:18,534
Something's wrong. I don't feel well.

141
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:21,412
In addition,
the sea level of Cape Canaveral

142
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:24,040
has a unique characteristic.

143
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:27,877
The sea level is described as "zero mark"
when measuring elevation.

144
00:10:28,377 --> 00:10:33,215
However, recent studies have revealed
that the sea's surface is not always zero.

145
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:36,969
For example, in the Indian Ocean
by the Maldives Archipelago,

146
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:41,349
the sea level curves down
by about 100 meters.

147
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:46,312
On the other hand, the Sea of Japan
curves up by 30 meters,

148
00:10:46,395 --> 00:10:50,149
and Cape Canaveral is
50 meters above the zero mark.

149
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,319
This could be due
to inconsistencies in gravity. 

150
00:10:53,402 --> 00:10:57,657
Cape Canaveral is one such location
with weaker gravity.

151
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:00,868
When tides are taken into account,

152
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:04,872
it is said that sea level may rise
by upwards of 100 meters.

153
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:06,957
Cape Canaveral

154
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:11,045
is the most suitable location
on Earth for a rocket launch.

155
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:21,013
Yikes, it's cold.

156
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:39,990
What?

157
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:47,081
What the… What happened to my cola?

158
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:58,926
STAND NAME: DIVER DRIVE
STAND MASTER: NARCISO ANASTASIA

159
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:10,813
So, Jolyne.

160
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:12,690
What is your plan?

161
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:16,527
Do you want to wait for
the Speedwagon Foundation and Mr. Jotaro?

162
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:21,532
Or do you want to keep
going after the priest?

163
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:23,826
I…

164
00:12:24,326 --> 00:12:26,704
Yes, we'll find him now.

165
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:30,541
Sorry, but we don't know
if your father will come in time.

166
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,918
He may not even come for two days.

167
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:37,047
Weather left the priest in shambles.

168
00:12:37,131 --> 00:12:38,883
His allies are all down.

169
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:40,634
The timing is impeccable.

170
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:43,137
The only thing for sure
is that if we don't hurry,

171
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:45,097
then we'd miss our chance.

172
00:12:52,271 --> 00:12:54,899
Hey Emporio, what are you doing?

173
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:56,609
Cut that out.

174
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:58,319
Why did you stop the car?

175
00:12:58,402 --> 00:12:59,945
I'm not trying to.

176
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:03,407
Hey! I said get the car moving.

177
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:05,117
This is a stolen car.

178
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:08,537
We are wanted criminals.
That hasn't changed.

179
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:11,999
- Also, a kid is in the driver's seat.
- That's not it.

180
00:13:12,082 --> 00:13:14,001
The car's acting up!

181
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:17,296
- What is it?
- I don't know, it suddenly slowed down!

182
00:13:32,102 --> 00:13:34,772
Ermes, switch with him.

183
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:40,945
Hey…

184
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:50,454
What are those things?

185
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:11,767
What's going on?

186
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:14,103
Brace for impact!

187
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:20,943
What's happening?

188
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:24,405
Cars! What the hell is going on?

189
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:27,116
Did a bad crash cause an explosion?

190
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:30,744
Emporio, pedal to the metal!
We need to go!

191
00:14:31,495 --> 00:14:32,955
I can't!

192
00:14:33,747 --> 00:14:35,499
It won't move!

193
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,042
The road is collapsing!

194
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:39,128
No, the road is fine.

195
00:14:39,211 --> 00:14:42,590
It's not collapsing,
and the guardrails are intact.

196
00:14:42,673 --> 00:14:44,592
There's no wind from an explosion!

197
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:53,475
You might think
I'm messing around, Jolyne,

198
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:55,978
but I'm holding on for my life.

199
00:14:56,061 --> 00:14:58,898
This car… This is bad!

200
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:03,193
Get out! You need to go!
This car isn't safe!

201
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:07,072
At this rate, we're going to fall!

202
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:09,700
We aren't falling down, but sideways!

203
00:15:10,534 --> 00:15:12,453
What do you mean, we're falling?

204
00:15:12,536 --> 00:15:15,039
The other cars fell already.

205
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:17,499
They slid down this road
as if it's a cliff!

206
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:20,336
The car is shaking!

207
00:15:20,419 --> 00:15:22,463
The front tires are in the air!

208
00:15:22,546 --> 00:15:24,882
Everyone, get out of the car!

209
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:28,636
Is this the priest's ability?

210
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:31,138
It's not the new moon yet.
How could this be?

211
00:15:31,221 --> 00:15:35,643
It's growing stronger,
the force is pulling us sideways!

212
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:36,894
Get out of the car, hurry!

213
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:39,063
It's going to flip backwards!

214
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:45,361
We're falling not down, but sideways.

215
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:47,196
How far will we fall?

216
00:15:49,865 --> 00:15:53,243
Jolyne! Don't let go of Emporio!

217
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:57,748
Diver Drive!

218
00:16:10,469 --> 00:16:12,096
Ermes!

219
00:16:12,638 --> 00:16:15,474
Stone Ocean!

220
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:17,685
How far did you fall, Ermes?

221
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:19,979
How far did you go?

222
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:21,981
Jolyne, we're going to fall!

223
00:16:22,064 --> 00:16:24,650
At this rate, we'll get hit by debris!

224
00:16:24,733 --> 00:16:26,860
Jolyne, forget Ermes for now.

225
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:29,029
If she survives, she'll find us.

226
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:30,656
But…

227
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,326
We've almost reached him,

228
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:38,330
but you'd rather retreat than find him?

229
00:16:38,414 --> 00:16:39,832
That's enough.

230
00:16:39,915 --> 00:16:43,085
Jolyne, your body won't last!

231
00:16:52,052 --> 00:16:55,014
How is this possible?

232
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:02,354
I can't believe this.

233
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:05,315
How can we fall sideways?

234
00:17:05,399 --> 00:17:08,068
Don't we have the ground
because of gravity?

235
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:10,946
This is what the priest
hoped to accomplish.

236
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:14,992
This is the power my father sealed
in Egypt 20 years ago.

237
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:19,663
This is what the priest called "heaven"!

238
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:25,377
Some trees aren't being uprooted.

239
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:29,590
Looks like the Visitor Center
is still in one piece.

240
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:31,925
Jolyne.

241
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:38,223
You said this is "heaven,"
but this might just be the beginning.

242
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:43,395
I have this feeling that
things will turn for the worse.

243
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:47,566
The priest is waiting for the new moon.

244
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:52,237
It plays a vital role in gravity,
and the new moon is only 36 hours away.

245
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:56,200
Listen, Jolyne,
Weather left the priest in a bad state.

246
00:17:56,283 --> 00:17:59,453
I know firsthand that he's hurt.

247
00:17:59,536 --> 00:18:03,332
Now's our chance to strike.
He's the one who's cornered.

248
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:07,711
Let's climb this guardrail
up to the Visitor Center.

249
00:18:08,754 --> 00:18:10,464
You're sure the priest is this way?

250
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:13,550
Yes. He's up ahead.

251
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:16,637
Go, Jolyne.

252
00:18:21,892 --> 00:18:24,353
Of course. My mind is made up.

253
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:30,734
That's right. Those eyes of yours, Jolyne.

254
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:32,861
Your face as you stare
far into the distance.

255
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:35,906
That's what makes my heart race.

256
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,492
Let's go, Emporio.

257
00:18:38,575 --> 00:18:39,576
Okay.

258
00:18:45,874 --> 00:18:47,709
Right now, your heart

259
00:18:47,793 --> 00:18:50,754
burns with the resolve to stop the priest.

260
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:54,633
At the same time, you're hoping
your father will come to save you.

261
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:59,429
I'm the one who can protect you,
not Weather, nor Jotaro.

262
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:06,061
In time, you'll begin to wish
that you were in my arms.

263
00:19:08,939 --> 00:19:13,068
In the beginning of all matter,
there was gravity.

264
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:15,070
Even for this earth,

265
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:18,157
gravity was its beginning.

266
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:26,331
Gravity keeps the planets revolving.

267
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:29,918
Where shall I head on this earth now?

268
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,670
What is going to transpire?

269
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:35,340
To my body and mind…

270
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:38,468
and to the end of all things?

271
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:43,682
Someone!

272
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:45,851
Someone, save us!

273
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:48,395
What in the world is going on?

274
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:50,981
What is happening?

275
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:54,568
Help!

276
00:19:54,651 --> 00:19:56,236
Someone, come save us!

277
00:20:03,952 --> 00:20:07,331
- Anyone!
- They're going to be all right.

278
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:08,707
No need to help them.

279
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:11,293
My phone doesn't have service.
It can't reach a tower!

280
00:20:11,376 --> 00:20:12,461
Why?

281
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:14,463
I can't even begin to guess.

282
00:20:15,047 --> 00:20:18,467
Maybe my phone is busted.

283
00:20:18,550 --> 00:20:20,969
It could also be caused
by this gravity thing,

284
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:22,804
but I really don't know.

285
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:27,142
Anyway, I have no idea
what's going on in other places.

286
00:20:27,851 --> 00:20:29,811
Are rescue teams on their way?

287
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:34,983
This is the ticketing office box, Jolyne.

288
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:37,611
That's the entrance

289
00:20:38,528 --> 00:20:41,114
to the Visitor Center.

290
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:44,785
Jolyne, the priest is still here, right?

291
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:52,000
Yes, he's close. He's almost within reach.

292
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:58,507
It's as if he was just here.

293
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:10,394
What?

294
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:18,360
This thing… it can't be!

295
00:21:18,443 --> 00:21:20,696
But why? What happened to it?

296
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:25,867
Pale Snake.

297
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:28,996
No, The Green Baby!

298
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:32,332
The priest's Stand evolved!

299
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:34,501
Unbelievable!

300
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:45,304
Jolyne!

301
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:52,352
My right hand!

302
00:21:54,896 --> 00:21:57,024
I came to finish you off now,

303
00:21:57,107 --> 00:21:59,318
if you can't wait two days.

304
00:22:05,532 --> 00:22:09,411
MARCH 21ST, 2012 11:23 A.M.

305
00:22:09,494 --> 00:22:14,249
36 HOURS AND 37 MINUTES UNTIL THE NEW MOON

306
00:23:41,128 --> 00:23:46,133
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
